      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Claire Denis's **White Material (2009)** (2009) stands as a haunting exploration of colonial collapse in an unnamed African nation, joining other unflinching examinations of post-colonial Africa like **I Dreamed of Africa** (2000) and **Nowhere in Africa** (2001). Through Isabelle Huppert's mesmerizing performance as Maria Vial, a French coffee plantation owner refusing to flee mounting civil unrest, Denis crafts a fever dream of privilege, denial, and inevitable catastrophe. The film's disorienting narrative structure mirrors Maria's psychological state, drawing influence from Denis's own childhood in colonial French Africa."
      },
