      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "**White Material** connects to a broader cinematic examination of post-colonial African identity, joining films like **District 9** (2009) and **Tsotsi** (2005) in exploring the complex legacy of European colonialism. Denis's film particularly excels in showing how personal delusion mirrors larger historical denial, with Maria's increasingly erratic behavior reflecting centuries of colonial cognitive dissonance."
